# Design component library first

Before you add or extend **user-facing UI** in `apps/core`, confirm there is **no good existing match** in our design stack. Do **not** default to raw `View` / `Pressable` / `StyleSheet` shells when a library primitive fits.

## Order of lookup (do this first)

1. **HeroUI Native** — `list_components` / `get_component_docs` on the **HeroUI Native MCP** (`user-heroui-native`), or `.heroui-docs/native/` + **`AGENTS.md`** after `heroui agents-md --native --output AGENTS.md`.
2. **Shared app components** — `apps/core/src/components/shared/` (e.g. `Screen`, `EmptyList`, `GuestAuthCard`, tab headers). Reuse or extend; do not duplicate.
3. **Product UX** — `docs/design/mobile-ux-master.md` for layout and copy patterns (with **i18n** via `useLocale` / `catalog.ts`).

Only after those fail to cover the need: compose from HeroUI compound parts (`Card.Body`, `Button`, `Chip`, `PressableFeedback`, …) with **`className`** / semantic variants — not a one-off “card” or “button” component.

**Protected actions (map):** Save/favorite, follow, and alerts require a signed-in user. Guests get the auth modal via `runMapProtectedAction` — do not wire favorite toggles or API calls without that gate (see `.cursor/rules/deelbaar-mobile-ux.mdc`).

## Good match → use it

| Need | Prefer |
|------|--------|
| Tappable surface with feedback | `PressableFeedback` or `Button` |
| Grouped content / list row | `Card` (+ `Card.Title` / `Card.Description`) or `Surface` |
| Badge, filter chip | `Chip` |
| Loading placeholder | `Skeleton` |
| Form field | `TextField`, `SearchField`, … per doc |
| Overlay / sheet | `BottomSheet`, `Dialog`, … per doc |

Match **compound anatomy and variants** from the official doc for that component (see `.cursor/rules/greenfield-heroui-core.mdc`).

## When custom RN is OK

- **No HeroUI primitive** for the job (e.g. Mapbox `MapView`) — wrap with `withUniwind`, HeroUI for chrome around it.
- **Layout-only** `View` wrappers inside an already doc-aligned HeroUI tree.
- **SDK-required** `style` props (map logo position, etc.) — not as a substitute for Card/Button/Chip.

## Anti-patterns (reject in review)

- Custom card/button shells that duplicate `Card` / `Button` styling (manual shadows, hardcoded colors, raw `Text` for labels).
- New `components/shared/*` that only re-wrap HeroUI without a clear, repeated product need.
- Skipping MCP/docs because “I know what Card looks like” — APIs and compound parts change.

